From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] align: provide a pool during global-ranking extension

The ordinary alignment path owns cfg.thread_pool while its workers extend
queries, then clears it.  Global-ranking post-processing instead extends
queries from a separate SimpleThreadPool after cfg.thread_pool has been
cleared.  extend_chunk nevertheless dereferences cfg.thread_pool
unconditionally, which aborts global-ranking tests when libstdc++ assertions
are enabled and is undefined behavior otherwise.

Use a per-call serial ThreadPool fallback when there is no outer alignment
pool.  Its pop-before-enqueue mode executes nested DP tasks on the calling
global-ranking worker, preserving the feature and results without sharing a
single nested task queue among concurrent query workers.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of DIAMOND 2.2.4 alignment code
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
---
 src/align/extend.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/align/extend.cpp b/src/align/extend.cpp
--- a/src/align/extend.cpp
+++ b/src/align/extend.cpp
@@ -219,7 +219,10 @@ static vector<Target> extend_chunk(BlockId query_id,
 	if (!flag_any(flags, DP::Flags::PARALLEL))
 		stat.inc(Statistics::TIME_CHAINING, timer.microseconds());
 
-	auto ret = align(targets, query_seq, cfg.query->ids()[query_id], query_cb, source_query_len, flags, hsp_values, cfg.extension_mode, *cfg.thread_pool, cfg, stat, pool);
+	ThreadPool serial_pool([](ThreadPool&, int64_t) {}, 0, 0, true);
+	ThreadPool& thread_pool = cfg.thread_pool ? *cfg.thread_pool : serial_pool;
+	auto ret = align(targets, query_seq, cfg.query->ids()[query_id], query_cb, source_query_len,
+		flags, hsp_values, cfg.extension_mode, thread_pool, cfg, stat, pool);
 	return ret;
 }
 
